1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,894
How many kilos of feed does one kilo of beef buy?

2
00:00:03,894 --> 00:00:05,294
In America in 1974:

3
00:00:05,294 --> 00:00:06,694
half a kilo.

4
00:00:06,694 --> 00:00:08,094
Today:

5
00:00:08,094 --> 00:00:09,494
more than two.

6
00:00:09,494 --> 00:00:12,519
Between those two numbers there is a pattern.

7
00:00:12,519 --> 00:00:13,919
America.

8
00:00:13,919 --> 00:00:15,319
Europe.

9
00:00:15,319 --> 00:00:15,840
Turkiye.

10
00:00:16,719 --> 00:00:15,840
Three continents, one wave.

11
00:00:18,534 --> 00:00:15,840
And it is running right now.

12
00:00:16,540 --> 00:00:18,213
The mechanism never changes.

13
00:00:18,213 --> 00:00:19,613
Feed gets expensive.

14
00:00:19,613 --> 00:00:21,013
Herds get slaughtered.

15
00:00:21,013 --> 00:00:23,840
And three years later, there is not enough beef.

16
00:00:24,540 --> 00:00:26,788
We start with America for one reason.

17
00:00:26,788 --> 00:00:28,551
Its record goes back to 1971.

18
00:00:28,551 --> 00:00:29,951
Fifty-five years.

19
00:00:29,951 --> 00:00:31,351
Nobody else has that.

20
00:00:31,351 --> 00:00:32,751
Nineteen seventy-two.

21
00:00:32,751 --> 00:00:38,463
The Soviet Union hides a failed harvest and quietly buys a quarter of the American wheat crop.

22
00:00:38,463 --> 00:00:39,863
Then the oil embargo.

23
00:00:39,863 --> 00:00:41,263
Corn tripled.

24
00:00:41,263 --> 00:00:43,750
And this line fell to the lowest point it has ever reached.

25
00:00:44,450 --> 00:00:45,850
Two thousand twelve.

26
00:00:45,850 --> 00:00:47,250
The Great Plains burned.

27
00:00:47,250 --> 00:00:50,260
Feed got expensive, so ranchers slaughtered the herd.

28
00:00:50,260 --> 00:00:52,191
Three years later beef was scarce,

29
00:00:52,191 --> 00:00:53,730
and the parity hit a record.

30
00:00:54,430 --> 00:00:55,974
Nineteen seventy-four.

31
00:00:55,974 --> 00:00:57,374
Ninety-six.

32
00:00:57,374 --> 00:00:58,777
Two thousand eleven.

33
00:00:58,777 --> 00:01:00,177
Twenty twenty-one.

34
00:01:00,177 --> 00:01:02,563
Four different decades, one curve.

35
00:01:02,563 --> 00:01:06,282
Three to four times higher, in forty to fifty months.

36
00:01:06,282 --> 00:01:07,030
Every single time.

37
00:01:07,730 --> 00:01:10,813
So does the rest of the world ride the same wave?

38
00:01:10,813 --> 00:01:12,213
Now we can check.

39
00:01:12,213 --> 00:01:13,613
Turkiye from 2010.

40
00:01:13,613 --> 00:01:15,013
Europe from 2015.

41
00:01:15,013 --> 00:01:16,413
This is not a race.

42
00:01:16,413 --> 00:01:19,497
Each country is measured against its own average.

43
00:01:19,497 --> 00:01:21,133
So where is America today?

44
00:01:21,133 --> 00:01:22,390
Eighty-four percent above its own.

45
00:01:23,090 --> 00:01:26,873
Twenty twenty-one was the first time the wave hit everyone at once.

46
00:01:26,873 --> 00:01:28,397
But not at the same moment.

47
00:01:28,397 --> 00:01:29,978
America bottomed out in May.

48
00:01:29,978 --> 00:01:31,389
Turkiye six months later,

49
00:01:31,389 --> 00:01:33,140
and the currency made it worse.

50
00:01:33,140 --> 00:01:34,607
Europe a full year behind.

51
00:01:34,607 --> 00:01:36,007
Same wave.

52
00:01:36,007 --> 00:01:36,890
Three different landfalls.

53
00:01:37,590 --> 00:01:39,274
So what does the feeder earn?

54
00:01:39,274 --> 00:01:41,480
Hold the calf and the overheads fixed,

55
00:01:41,480 --> 00:01:42,880
and only feed moves.

56
00:01:42,880 --> 00:01:45,261
On that basis, all three are green today.

57
00:01:45,261 --> 00:01:47,932
But in America the calf itself is at a record.

58
00:01:47,932 --> 00:01:50,835
The real margin is thinner than this chart admits.

59
00:01:50,835 --> 00:01:52,635
Parity gives you the direction.

60
00:01:52,635 --> 00:01:53,750
Not the whole bill.

61
00:01:54,450 --> 00:01:56,392
The wave is the same everywhere.

62
00:01:56,392 --> 00:01:57,792
The shield is not.

63
00:01:57,792 --> 00:02:00,279
America locks the margin on the exchange.

64
00:02:00,279 --> 00:02:02,524
Europe cashes a cheque from Brussels.

65
00:02:02,524 --> 00:02:05,012
The Turkish feeder has no futures market.

66
00:02:05,012 --> 00:02:06,412
No margin insurance.

67
00:02:06,412 --> 00:02:08,111
And credit at fifty percent.

68
00:02:08,111 --> 00:02:09,080
Same wave.

69
00:02:09,511 --> 00:02:09,080
No shield.

70
00:02:09,780 --> 00:02:11,184
So where are we now?

71
00:02:11,184 --> 00:02:12,584
At the top.

72
00:02:12,584 --> 00:02:16,514
The highest parity America has seen in fifty-five years.

73
00:02:16,514 --> 00:02:19,251
Every previous peak ended the same way:

74
00:02:19,251 --> 00:02:22,831
herds rebuild, supply returns, and the ratio falls.

75
00:02:22,831 --> 00:02:24,726
It has happened four times.

76
00:02:24,726 --> 00:02:26,126
This is the fifth.

77
00:02:26,126 --> 00:02:28,021
You cannot shrink the wave.

78
00:02:28,021 --> 00:02:29,050
You can only price it.
